 flame. I pour some ground coffee into the pot, ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,38,16","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,38,16,0","type":4,"elements":"enough to make sure the resulting brew will be good and strong, and set it on the stove to boil.","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,39","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,39,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,39,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,40","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,0,0","type":4,"elements":"Haymitch is still dead to the world. Since nothing else has worked, I fill a basin with icy cold water, dump it on ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,40,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,1,0","type":4,"elements":"his head, and spring out of the way. A guttural animal sound comes from his throat. He jumps up, kicking his ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,40,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,2,0","type":4,"elements":"chair ten feet behind him and wielding a knife. I forgot he always sleeps with one clutched in his hand. I should ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,40,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,3,0","type":4,"elements":"have pried it from his fingers, but I've had a lot on my mind. Spewing profanity, he slashes the air a few ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,40,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,4,0","type":4,"elements":"moments before coming to his senses. He wipes his face on his shirtsleeve and turns to the windowsill where I ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,40,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,5,0","type":4,"elements":"perch, just in case I need to make a quick exit. \"What are you doing?\" he sputters. \"You told me to wake you an ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,40,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,6,0","type":4,"elements":"hour before the cameras come,\" I say. \"What?\" he says. \"Your idea,\" I insist. He seems to remember. \"Why am I ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,40,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,7,0","type":4,"elements":"all wet?\" \"I couldn't shake you awake,\" I say. \"Look, if you wanted to be babied, you should have asked Peeta.\" ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,40,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,40,8,0","type":4,"elements":"\"Asked me what?\" Just the sound of his voice twists my","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,41","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,0,0","type":4,"elements":"stomach into a knot of unpleasant emotions like guilt, sadness, and fear. And longing. I might as well admit ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,41,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,1,0","type":4,"elements":"there's some of that, too. Only it has too much competition to ever win out. I watch as Peeta crosses to the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,41,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,2,0","type":4,"elements":"table, the sunlight from the window picking up the glint of fresh snow in his blond hair. He looks strong and ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,41,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,3,0","type":4,"elements":"healthy, so different from the sick, starving boy I knew in the arena, and you can barely even notice his limp ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,41,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,4,0","type":4,"elements":"now. He sets a loaf of fresh-baked bread on the table and holds out his hand to Haymitch. \"Asked you to wake ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,41,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,5,0","type":4,"elements":"me without giving me pneumonia,\" says Haymitch, passing over his knife. He pulls off his filthy shirt, revealing ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,41,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,6,0","type":4,"elements":"an equally soiled undershirt, and rubs himself down with the dry part. Peeta smiles and douses Haymitch's ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,41,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,7,0","type":4,"elements":"knife in white liquor from a bottle on the floor. He wipes the blade clean on his shirttail and slices the bread. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,41,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,41,8,0","type":4,"elements":"Peeta keeps all of us in fresh baked goods. I hunt. He bakes. Haymitch","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,42","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,42,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,42,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,43","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,43,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,43,0,0","type":4,"elements":"drinks. We have our own ways to stay busy, to keep thoughts of our time as contestants in the Hunger Games","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,44","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,44,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,44,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,45","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,45,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,45,0,0","type":4,"elements":"at bay. It's not until he's handed Haymitch the heel that he even looks at me for the first time. \"Would you like a ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,45,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,45,1,0","type":4,"elements":"piece?\" \"No, I ate at the Hob,\" 