a29d"}]},{"id":"0,545,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,545,7,0","type":4,"elements":"voice. '\"Take his place, Haymitch, because all things being equal, I'd rather Peeta had a crack at the rest of his ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,545,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,545,8,0","type":4,"elements":"life than you? I bite my lip because once he's said it, I'm afraid","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,546","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,0,0","type":4,"elements":"that's what I do want. For Peeta to live, even if it means Haymitch's death. No, I don't. He's dreadful, of course, ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,546,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,1,0","type":4,"elements":"but Haymitch is my family now. What did I come for? I think. What could I possibly want here? \"I came for a ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,546,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,2,0","type":4,"elements":"drink,\" I say. Haymitch bursts out laughing and slams the bottle on the table before me. I run my sleeve across ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,546,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,3,0","type":4,"elements":"the top and take a couple gulps before I come up choking. It takes a few minutes to compose myself, and even ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,546,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,4,0","type":4,"elements":"then my eyes and nose are still streaming. But inside me, the liquor feels like fire and I like it. \"Maybe it should ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,546,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,5,0","type":4,"elements":"be you,\" I say matter-of-factly as I pull up a chair. \"You hate life, anyway.\" \"Very true,\" says Haymitch. \"And ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,546,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,6,0","type":4,"elements":"since last time I tried to keep you alive... seems like I'm obligated to save the boy this time.\" \"That's another ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,546,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,7,0","type":4,"elements":"good point,\" I say, wiping my nose and tipping up the bottle again. \"Peeta's argument is that since I chose you, I ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,546,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,546,8,0","type":4,"elements":"now owe him. Anything he wants. And what he wants is the","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,547","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,547,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,547,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,548","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,0,0","type":4,"elements":"chance to go in again to protect you,\" says Haymitch. I knew it. In this way, Peeta's not hard to predict. While I ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,1,0","type":4,"elements":"was wallowing around on the floor of that cellar, thinking only of myself, he was here, thinking only of me. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,2,0","type":4,"elements":"Shame isn't a strong enough word for what I feel. \"You could live a hundred lifetimes and not deserve him, you ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,3,0","type":4,"elements":"know,\" Haymitch says. \"Yeah, yeah,\" I say brusquely. \"No question, he's the superior one in this trio. So, what ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,4,0","type":4,"elements":"are you going to do?\" \"I don't know.\" Haymitch sighs. \"Go back in with you maybe, if I can. If my name's drawn ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,5,0","type":4,"elements":"at the reaping, it won't matter. He'll just volunteer to take my place.\" We sit for a while in silence. \"It'd be bad for ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,6,0","type":4,"elements":"you in the arena, wouldn't it? Knowing all the others?\" I ask. \"Oh, I think we can count on it being unbearable ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,7,0","type":4,"elements":"wherever I am.\" He nods at the bottle. \"Can I have that back now?\" \"No,\" I say, wrapping my arms around it. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,8,0","type":4,"elements":"Haymitch pullsanother bottle out from under the table and gives the top a twist. But I realize I am not just here ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,9","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,9,0","type":4,"elements":"for a drink. There's something else I want from Haymitch. \"Okay, I figured out what I'm asking,\" I say. \"If it is ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,10","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,10,0","type":4,"elements":"Peeta and me in the Games, this time we try to keep him alive.\" Something flickers across his bloodshot eyes. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,11","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,11,0","type":4,"elements":"Pain. \"Like you said, it's going to be bad no matter how you slice it. And whatever Peeta wants, it's his turn to ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,12","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,12,0","type":4,"elements":"be saved. We both owe him that.\" My voice takes on a pleading tone. \"Besides, the Capitol hates me so much, ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,13","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,13,0","type":4,"elements":"I'm as good as dead now. He still might have a chance. Please, Haymitch. Say you'll help me.\" He frowns at his ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,14","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,14,0","type":4,"elements":"bottle, weighing my words. \"All right,\" he says finally. \"Thanks,\" I say. I should go see Peeta now, but I don't ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,15","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,15,0","type":4,"elements":"want to. My head's spinning from the drink, and I'm so wiped out, who knows what he could get me to agree ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,548,16","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,548,16,0","type":4,"elements":"to? No, now I have to go home to face my mother and Prim. As I stagger up the steps to my","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,549","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,549,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,549,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,550","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,0,0","type":4,"elements":"house, the front door opens and Gale pulls me into his arms. \"I was wrong. We should have gone when you ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,550,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,1,0","type":4,"elements":"said,\" he whispers. \"No,\" I say. I'm having trouble focusing, and liquor keeps sloshing out of my bottle and down ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,550,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,2,0","type":4,"elements":"the back of Gale's jacket, but he doesn't seem to care. \"It's not too late,\" he says. Over his shoulder, I see my ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,550,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,3,0","type":4,"elements":"mother and Prim clutching each other in the doorway. We run. They die. And now I've got Peeta to protect. End ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,550,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,4,0","type":4,"elements":"of discussion. \"Yeah, it is.\" My knees give way and he's holding me up. As the alcohol overcomes my mind, I ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,550,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,5,0","type":4,"elements":"hear the glass bottle shatter on the floor. This seems appropriate since I have obviously lost my grip on ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,550,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,6,0","type":4,"elements":"everything. When I wake up, I barely get to the toilet before the white liquor makes its reappearance. It burns ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,550,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,7,0","type":4,"elements":"just as much coming up as it did going down, and tastes twice as bad. I'm trembling and sweaty when I finish ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,550,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,550,8,0","type":4,"elements":"vomiting, but at least most of the stuff is out of my system. Enough made it","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,551","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,0,0","type":4,"elements":"into my bloodstream, though, to result in a pounding headache, parched mouth, and boiling stomach. I turn on ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,551,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,1,0","type":4,"elements":"the shower and stand under the warm rain for a minute before I realize I'm still in my underclothes. My mother ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,551,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,2,0","type":4,"elements":"must have just stripped off my filthy outer ones and tucked me in bed. I throw the wet undergarments into the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,551,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,3,0","type":4,"elements":"sink and pour shampoo on my head. My hands sting, and that's when I notice the stitches, small and even, ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,551,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,4,0","type":4,"elements":"across one palm and up the side of the other hand. Vaguely I remember breaking that glass window last night. I ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,551,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,5,0","type":4,"elements":"scrub myself from head to toe, only stopping to throw up again right in the shower. It's mostly just bile and goes ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,551,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,6,0","type":4,"elements":"down the drain with the sweet-smelling bubbles. Finally clean, I pull on my robe and head back to bed, ignoring ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,551,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,7,0","type":4,"elements":"my dripping hair. I climb under the blankets, sure this is what it must feel like to be poisoned. The footsteps on ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,551,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,551,8,0","type":4,"elements":"the stairs renew my panic from last night.","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,552","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,552,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,552,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,553","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,553,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,553,0,0","type":4,"elements":"I'm not ready to see my mother and Prim. I have to pull myself together to be calm and reassuring, the way I","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,554","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,554,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,554,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,555","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,555,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,555,0,0","type":4,"elements":"was when we said our good-byes the day of the last reaping. I have to be strong. I struggle into an upright ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,555,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,555,1,0","type":4,"elements":"position, push my wet hair off my throbbing temples, and brace myself for this meeting. They appear in the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,555,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,555,2,0","type":4,"elements":"doorway, holding tea and toast, their faces filled with concern. I open my mouth, planning to start off with some ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,555,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,555,3,0","type":4,"elements":"kind of joke, and burst into tears. So much for being strong. My mother sits on the side of the bed and Prim ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,555,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,555,4,0","type":4,"elements":"crawls right up next to me and they hold me, making quiet soothing sounds, until I am mostly cried out. Then ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,555,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,555,5,0","type":4,"elements":"Prim gets a towel and dries my hair, combing out the knots, while my mother coaxes tea and toast into me. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,555,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,555,6,0","type":4,"elements":"They dress me in warm pajamas and layer more blankets on me and I drift off again. I can tell by the","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,556","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,556,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,556,0,0","type":4,"elements":"light it's late afternoon when I come round again. There's a glass of water on my bedside table and I gulp it ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,556,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,556,1,0","type":4,"elements":"down thirstily. My stomach and head still","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,557","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,557,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,557,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,558","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,558,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,558,0,0","type":4,"elements":"feel rocky, but much better than they did earlier. I rise, dress, and braid back my hair. Before I go down, I pause ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,558,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,558,1,0","type":4,"elements":"at the top of the stairs, feeling slightly embarrassed about the way I've handled the news of the Quarter Quell. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,558,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,558,2,0","type":4,"elements":"My erratic flight, drinking with Haymitch, weeping. Given the circumstances, I guess I deserve one day of ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,558,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,558,3,0","type":4,"elements":"indulgence. I'm glad the cameras weren't here for it, though. Downstairs, my mother and Prim embrace me ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,558,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,558,4,0","type":4,"elements":"again, but they're not overly emotional. I know they're holding things in to make it easier on me. Looking at ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,558,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,558,5,0","type":4,"elements":"Prim's face, it's hard to imagine she's the same frail little girl I left behind on reaping day nine months ago. The ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,558,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,558,6,0","type":4,"elements":"combination of that ordeal and all that has","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,559","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,559,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,559,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,560","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,0,0","type":4,"elements":"followed--the cruelty in the district, the parade of sick and wounded that she often treats by herself now if my ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,560,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,1,0","type":4,"elements":"mother's hands are too full -- these things have aged her years. She's grown quite a bit, too; we're practically ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,560,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,2,0","type":4,"elements":"the same height now, but that isn't what makes her seem so much older. My mother ladles out a mug of broth ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,560,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,3,0","type":4,"elements":"for me, and I ask for a second mug to take to Haymitch. Then I walk across the lawn to his house. He's only ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,560,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,4,0","type":4,"elements":"just waking up and accepts the mug without comment. We sit there, almost peacefully, sipping our broth and ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,560,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,5,0","type":4,"elements":"watching the sun set through his living room window. I hear someone walking around upstairs and I assume it's ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,560,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,6,0","type":4,"elements":"Hazelle, but a few minutes later Peeta comes down and tosses a cardboard box of empty liquor bottles on the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,560,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,7,0","type":4,"elements":"table with finality. \"There, it's done,\" he says. It's taking all of Haymitch's resources to focus his eyes on the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,560,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,560,8,0","type":4,"elements":"bottles, so I speak up. \"What's done?\" \"I've poured all the liquor down","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,561","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,0,0","type":4,"elements":"the drain,\" says Peeta. This seems to jolt Haymitch out of his stupor, and he paws through the box in disbelief. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,561,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,1,0","type":4,"elements":"\"You what?\" \"I tossed the lot,\" says Peeta. \"He'll just buy more,\" I say. \"No, he won't,\" says Peeta. \"I tracked ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,561,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,2,0","type":4,"elements":"down Ripper this morning and told her I'd turn her in the second she sold to either of you. I paid her off, too, just ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,561,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,3,0","type":4,"elements":"for good measure, but I don't think she's eager to be back in the Peacekeepers' custody.\" Haymitch takes a ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,561,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,4,0","type":4,"elements":"swipe with his knife but Peeta deflects it so easily it's pathetic. Anger rises up in me. \"What business is it of ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,561,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,5,0","type":4,"elements":"yours what he does?\" \"It's completely my business. However it falls out, two of us are going to be in the arena ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,561,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,6,0","type":4,"elements":"again with the other as mentor. We can't afford any drunkards on this team. Especially not you, Katniss,\" says ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,561,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,7,0","type":4,"elements":"Peeta to me. \"What?\" I sputter indignantly. It would be more convincing if I weren't still so hungover. \"Last ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,561,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,561,8,0","type":4,"elements":"night's the only time I've ever even been drunk.\" \"Yeah, and look at the","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,562","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,562,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,562,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,563","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,563,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,563,0,0","type":4,"elements":"shape you're in,\" says Peeta. I don't know what I expected from my first meeting with Peeta after the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,563,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,563,1,0","type":4,"elements":"announcement. A few hugs and kisses. A little comfort maybe. Not this. I turn to Haymitch. \"Don't worry, I'll get ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,563,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,563,2,0","type":4,"elements":"you more liquor.\" \"Then I'll turn you both in. Let you sober up in the stocks,\" says Peeta. \"What's the","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,564","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,564,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,564,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,565","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,565,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,565,0,0","type":4,"elements":"point to this?\" asks Haymitch. \"The point is that two of us are coming home from the Capitol. One mentor and ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,565,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,565,1,0","type":4,"elements":"one victor,\" says Peeta. \"Effie's sending me recordings of all the living victors. We're going to watch their ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,565,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,565,2,0","type":4,"elements":"Games and learn everything we can about how they fight. We're going to put on weight and get strong. We're ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,565,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,565,3,0","type":4,"elements":"going to start acting like Careers. And one of us is going to be victor again whether you two like it or not!\" He ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,565,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,565,4,0","type":4,"elements":"sweeps out of the room, slamming the front door. Haymitch and I wince at the bang. \"I don't","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,566","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,0,0","type":4,"elements":"like self-righteous people,\" I say. \"What's to like?\" says Haymitch, who begins sucking the dregs out of the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,566,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,1,0","type":4,"elements":"empty bottles. \"You and me. That's who he plans on coming home,\" I say. \"Well, then the joke's on him,\" says ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,566,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,2,0","type":4,"elements":"Haymitch. But after a few days, we agree to act like Careers, because this is the best way to get Peeta ready ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,566,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,3,0","type":4,"elements":"as well. Every night we watch the old recaps of the Games that the remaining victors won. I realize we never ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,566,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,4,0","type":4,"elements":"met any of them on the Victory Tour, which seems odd in retrospect. When I bring it up, Haymitch says the last ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,566,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,5,0","type":4,"elements":"thing President Snow would've wanted was to show Peeta and me--especially me -- bonding with other victors ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,566,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,6,0","type":4,"elements":"in potentially rebellious districts. Victors have a special status, and if they appeared to be supporting my ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,566,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,7,0","type":4,"elements":"defiance of the Capitol, it would've been dangerous politically. Adjusting for age, I realize some of our ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,566,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,566,8,0","type":4,"elements":"opponents may be elderly, which is both sad and reassuring. Peeta takes copious notes,","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,567","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,567,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,567,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,568","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,0,0","type":4,"elements":"Haymitch volunteers information about the victors' personalities, and slowly we begin to know our competition. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,568,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,1,0","type":4,"elements":"Every morning we do exercises to strengthen our bodies. We run and lift things and stretch our muscles. Every ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,568,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,2,0","type":4,"elements":"afternoon we work on combat skills, throwing knives, fighting hand to hand; I even teach them to climb trees. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,568,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,3,0","type":4,"elements":"Officially, tributes aren't supposed to train, but no one tries to stop us. Even in regular years, the tributes from ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,568,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,4,0","type":4,"elements":"Districts 1, 2, and 4 show up able to wield spears and swords. This is nothing by comparison. After all the years ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,568,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,5,0","type":4,"elements":"of abuse, Haymitch's body resists improvement. He's still remarkably strong, but the shortest run winds him. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,568,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,6,0","type":4,"elements":"And you'd think a guy who sleeps every night with a knife might actually be able to hit the side of a house with ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,568,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,7,0","type":4,"elements":"one, but his hands shake so badly it takes weeks for him to achieve even that. Peeta and I excel under the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,568,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,568,8,0","type":4,"elements":"new regimen, though. It gives me something to do. It","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,569","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,569,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,569,0,0","type":4,"elements":"gives us all something to do besides accept defeat. My mother puts us on a special diet to gain weight. Prim ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,569,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,569,1,0","type":4,"elements":"treats our sore muscles. Madge sneaks us her father's Capitol newspapers. Predictions on who will be victor of ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,569,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,569,2,0","type":4,"elements":"the victors show us among the favorites. Even Gale steps into the picture on Sundays, although he's got no ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,569,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,569,3,0","type":4,"elements":"love for Peeta or Haymitch, and teaches us all he knows about snares. It's weird for me, being in conversations ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,569,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,569,4,0","type":4,"elements":"with both Peeta and Gale, but they seem to have set aside whatever issues they have about me.","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,570","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,570,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,570,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,571","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,571,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,571,0,0","type":4,"elements":"One night, as I'm walking Gale back into town, he even admits, \"It'd be better if he were easier to hate.\" \"Tell me ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,571,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,571,1,0","type":4,"elements":"about it,\" I say. \"If I could've just hated him in the arena, we all wouldn't be in this mess now. He'd be dead, and ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,571,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,571,2,0","type":4,"elements":"I'd be a happy little victor all by myself.\" \"And where would we be,","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,572","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,572,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,572,0,0","type":4,"elements":"","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,573","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,0,0","type":4,"elements":"Katniss?\" asks Gale. I pause, not knowing what to say. Where would I be with my pretend cousin who wouldn't ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,573,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,1,0","type":4,"elements":"be my cousin if it weren't for Peeta? Would he have still kissed me and would I have kissed him back had I ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,573,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,2,0","type":4,"elements":"been free to do so? Would I have let myself open up to him, lulled by the security of money and food and the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,573,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,3,0","type":4,"elements":"illusion of safety being a victor could bring under different circumstances? But there would still always be the ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,573,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,4,0","type":4,"elements":"reaping looming over us, over our children. No matter what I wanted ... \"Hunting. Like every Sunday,\" I say. I ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,573,5","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,5,0","type":4,"elements":"know he didn't mean the question literally, but this is as much as I can honestly give. Gale knows I chose him ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,573,6","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,6,0","type":4,"elements":"over Peeta when I didn't make a run for it. To me, there's no point in talking about things that might have been. ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,573,7","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,7,0","type":4,"elements":"Even if I had killed Peeta in the arena, I still wouldn't have wanted to marry anyone. I only got engaged to save ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,573,8","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,573,8,0","type":4,"elements":"people's lives, and that completely backfired. I'm afraid, anyway, that any kind","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]}],"format_name":"Text body"},{"id":"0,574","type":2,"elements":[{"id":"0,574,0","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,574,0,0","type":4,"elements":"of emotional scene with Gale might cause him to do something drastic. Like start that uprising in the mines. And ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,574,1","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,574,1,0","type":4,"elements":"as Haymitch says, District 12 isn't ready for that. If anything, they're less ready than before the Quarter Quell ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,574,2","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,574,2,0","type":4,"elements":"announcement, because the following morning another hundred Peacekeepers arrived on the train. Since I ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,574,3","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,574,3,0","type":4,"elements":"don't plan on making it back alive a second time, the sooner Gale lets me go, the better. I do plan on saying ","format_id":"93e3f29c-098d-4872-9ef8-405c14e5a29d"}]},{"id":"0,574,4","type":3,"elements":[{"id":"0,574,4,0","type":4,"elements":"one or two things to him after the reaping, when we're allowed an hour for good-byes. 